"""Apply the October 2026 public interpretation additions."""
from pathlib import Path
import re
ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "dist"
guide = "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/guide-to-contributory-factors-for-reported-road-casualty-statistics/guide-to-contributory-factors-for-reported-road-casualties-great-britain"
index = (ROOT / "index.html").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
bikes = (ROOT / "bikes.html").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
header = bikes.split("<main")[0].replace('<a href="bikes.html" class="active" aria-current="page">', '<a href="bikes.html">')
header = re.sub(r"<title>.*?</title>", "<title>Understanding the evidence | Motorcycle Evidence</title>", header)
header = re.sub(r'<meta name="description" content="[^"]*">', '<meta name="description" content="A plain-English guide to motorcycle casualty patterns, uncertainty and the evidence needed to explain them.">', header)
header = header.replace('<script src="bikes.js" defer></script>', "")
header = header.replace("</nav>", '<a href="evidence.html" class="active" aria-current="page">Understanding the evidence</a></nav>')
body = """<main id="main">
<section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM PATTERNS TO EXPLANATIONS</p><h1>What can the numbers tell us?</h1><p class="lede">Who is being hurt, where it happens and which questions deserve closer investigation. Explaining why needs more evidence.</p></div></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>The essentials, in plain English</h2><div class="two-col"><div><h3>Counts show the scale of the problem</h3><p>KSI means killed or seriously injured. A group with more KSI casualties contributes more to the recorded injury burden. It may also contain more riders or cover more miles.</p><h3>A percentage needs a denominator</h3><p>“KSI among casualties” describes how severe the recorded injuries were. It is not the chance of crashing, or the risk per journey. Comparing that risk needs suitable mileage or other exposure data.</p></div><div><h3>Age is not riding experience</h3><p>A rider aged 35–44 or 65+ may be experienced, newly qualified or returning after a break. These records do not identify which. A “returning rider” explanation is a research question.</p><h3>An observed rise is not an explanation</h3><p>Changes can reflect riding activity, population mix, reporting and ordinary year-to-year variation. A time coincidence does not show that advice, training or technology caused a change.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What we can examine now</h2><p>The existing explorer combines age and motorcycle category with these recorded circumstances. These describe events and surroundings; they are not police-assessed contributory factors.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Recorded information</th><th scope="col">Useful question</th><th scope="col">What it cannot establish</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Junction and urban/rural setting</th><td>Where are casualties concentrated?</td><td>Who failed to observe or give way</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Skidding and overturning</th><td>Which groups have these events recorded?</td><td>Wheel lock, incorrect braking or ABS activation</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Posted speed limit</th><td>On what kinds of roads do injuries occur?</td><td>The bike's travelling or impact speed</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Historic bend manoeuvre</th><td>Which records identify a bend manoeuvre?</td><td>All bend collisions: newer coding leaves gaps</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p><a href="./#explore">Explore these circumstances →</a> · <a href="bikes.html">Compare motorcycles and age →</a></p><p>Our source files also contain weather, lighting, road surface, objects struck and leaving the carriageway. These could support further breakdowns; not every source field is currently exposed as a chart.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><p class="eyebrow">ADDITIONAL DATA NEEDED</p><h2>Contributory factors: the next evidence to add</h2><div class="notice"><strong>Not yet included in this site’s record-level analysis.</strong> Detailed contributory / road safety factors are absent from our open-data extracts. Access requires a DfT application and data-use agreement. No request has been submitted through this site.</div>
<p>Relevant assessments cover braking unsuitable for conditions, poor manoeuvres, observation, experience, speed, distraction and impairment. These would help us investigate rider-control and hazard-response questions. They would not supply measured reaction times or brake inputs.</p>
<p>We need to distinguish a factor assigned to the motorcyclist from one assigned to another participant. Several factors may apply to one collision; missing factors do not mean no contributing problems existed. These are police assessments, not definitive findings of causation.</p>
<p>The older contributory-factor system is being replaced by road safety factors. Recording changes can create apparent trends, so comparisons must account for the reporting system and police-force coverage.</p>
<p><a href="GUIDE">DfT definitions, limitations and access arrangements</a> · <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/statistical-data-sets/road-safety-statistics-data-tables">Published summary tables</a></p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What might explain the age patterns?</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Possible explanation</th><th scope="col">Evidence needed to test it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">More riding in particular age groups</th><td>Age-specific mileage, rider numbers and trip patterns</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Returning after a riding break</th><td>Riding history, time away, recent mileage and familiarisation</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Different motorcycles or unfamiliar controls</th><td>Verified model, safety-system fitment, ownership history and rider familiarity</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Braking, observation or avoidance difficulties</th><td>Participant-linked factors and instrumented tests of braking, steering and response time</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Effects of advice or training</th><td>Who received it, when, changes in behaviour and suitable comparison groups</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p>These are hypotheses, not findings that any particular organisation, training approach or technology caused casualties.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>How certain are the changes?</h2><p>The recorded counts are the observed totals. Statistical intervals describe variation under a model; they do not fix missing records or biased reporting. Wide intervals mean the data leave substantial uncertainty about the underlying change.</p><p>The age table now shows individual 95% uncertainty intervals and tests adjusted for examining multiple age groups. A ratio of 1 means unchanged counts; 1.5 means a 50% rise. A result that does not meet a statistical threshold can still warrant investigation, and a result that does meet it does not establish a cause.</p><p><a href="./#findings">View the age comparisons and methods →</a></p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Research priorities</h2><ol><li>Use age, capacity and recorded circumstances to define focused questions.</li><li>Obtain participant-linked factor data through DfT and check coverage and recording changes.</li><li>Collect riding histories to distinguish returning riders from continuous riders.</li><li>Use controlled, instrumented studies to measure braking into turns, hazard avoidance and cue-to-action response time.</li></ol><p class="small">Interpretation updated 20 October 2026. Analysis: Dr Owen Williams · MotoEng / UWTSD.</p></section>
</main><footer><div><strong>Motorcycle Evidence</strong><span>Dr Owen Williams · MotoEng / UWTSD</span></div><a href="./#methods">Sources & methods</a></footer></body></html>""".replace("GUIDE", guide)
(ROOT / "evidence.html").write_text(header + body, encoding="utf-8")
for name, content in [("index.html", index), ("bikes.html", bikes)]:
    content = content.replace("</nav>", '<a href="evidence.html">Understanding the evidence</a></nav>')
    content = content.replace('<main id="main">', '<main id="main"><p class="notice"><strong>New to the statistics?</strong> <a href="evidence.html">Read the plain-English guide to patterns, possible explanations and missing evidence.</a></p>')
    if name == "index.html":
        content = content.replace("Small counts fluctuate substantially. This is a screening table for follow-up, not a ranking of causal effects.", "Riders and passengers combined, all capacities; independent of explorer filters. The table reports observed changes and uncertainty, not changes in risk per mile.")
        content = content.replace('<div id="change-table" class="table-wrap"></div>', '''<div id="change-table" class="table-wrap"></div><p id="uncertainty-summary"></p><details><summary>How to read the uncertainty and significance results</summary><p>A ratio of 1 means equal counts; 1.5 means a 50% rise. Individual 95% intervals use an exact conditional Poisson comparison. “Adjusted p” uses Holm’s method across all nine age categories, including unknown age, to reduce false positives when screening multiple groups. The individual intervals are not adjusted for multiple comparisons.</p><p>The model assumes independent Poisson counts and equal one-year periods. People in the same collision may be correlated. It does not account for exposure, reporting bias, changing demographics or other explanations. These exploratory results are not confirmatory tests of a pre-specified returning-rider hypothesis. No age-specific mileage denominator is available.</p><p><a href="data/uncertainty.json" download>Download counts, intervals and test results</a></p></details>''')
    (ROOT / name).write_text(content, encoding="utf-8")
app = (ROOT / "app.js").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
start = app.index(" const rr=data.explorer.rows.filter")
end = app.index("\n}", start)
app = app[:start] + """ const comparison=data.uncertainty.rows;
 const interval=r=>r.low===null?'Not estimable':r.low.toFixed(2)+'–'+(r.high===null?'∞':r.high.toFixed(2));
 $('change-table').innerHTML=table(['Casualty age','2024 fatal','2025 fatal','Count change','2025 / 2024 ratio','Individual 95% interval','Adjusted p','Interpretation'],comparison.map(r=>[r.age,n(r.before),n(r.after),r.before?dec.format(100*(r.after/r.before-1))+'%':'Not defined',r.ratio===null?'Not defined':r.ratio.toFixed(2),interval(r),r.p_holm.toFixed(3),r.before+r.after===0?'No events':r.p_holm<.05?'Meets 5% adjusted threshold':'Does not meet 5% adjusted threshold']));
 const significant=comparison.filter(r=>r.p_holm<.05);
 $('uncertainty-summary').textContent=significant.length?significant.map(r=>r.age).join(', ')+' meet the 5% threshold after adjustment across age groups. This does not establish why counts changed.':'No age group meets the 5% threshold after adjustment across age groups. The rises in the 35–44 and 65+ groups remain research leads, not established effects or proof of returning-rider involvement.';
""" + app[end:]
app = app.replace("['explorer','labels','annual','history','claims','audit']", "['explorer','labels','annual','history','claims','audit','uncertainty']")
(ROOT / "app.js").write_text(app, encoding="utf-8")
print("Updated evidence guide, navigation and age uncertainty table.")
